Keep a translator's FAIL for a later job on the same inputs (waste audit 2, row 23): core/translate_stage.
A translated attempt 0 that FAILs is kept in the ledger row as "translated_fail", under a key of everything the
translator and the judge read (the translator's revision, the verdict_memo key, every packet file, the function
bodies). A later job of that function (a requeue, or tools/translate_backlog.py --record, which now records FAILs)
takes the kept attempt instead of translating and judging the same C again. A PASS, a tamper, a "-dirty" or unknown
revision keep none.
Proof: docs/proofs/2026-10-23/PROOFS.md proof F: 97 Skies functions, the same verdict, score, summary and first
differences in all three runs (89 PASS, 8 FAIL); the later job took all 8 FAILs, 10.3 -> 0.21 s for them.
It changes when the judge runs, so it is the user's call with the judge set.
Apply: git apply docs/proposals/translated_fail_memo.patch   Undo: git apply -R docs/proposals/translated_fail_memo.patch

